{"reference":"Revelation 4","book":"Revelation","chapter":4,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"Reading the Vision’s Imagery","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The throne and the four living creatures belong to a pattern that many readers understand as Revelation’s reworking of Ezekielian imagery. Similar throne, creature, scroll, measuring, witness, plague, Gog, battle, city, river, and tree imagery recurs across Revelation in its own literary sequence.","verse_refs":["Revelation 4:1-11"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_004_f5a145de9b969fcb3fd24858"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]},{"kind":"surrounding_passages","title":"The Wider Book","blocks":[{"id":"block_2","text":"Across Revelation, many readers see repeated reworkings of Israel’s Scriptures, especially Daniel, Ezekiel, Isaiah, Exodus, Zechariah, Genesis, and Psalms. This broader pattern provides context for reading the book’s visions as a connected sequence of scriptural imagery rather than as isolated scenes.","verse_refs":["Revelation 10:1-11","Revelation 11:1-19","Revelation 12:1-17","Revelation 13:1-18","Revelation 14:1-20","Revelation 15:1-8","Revelation 16:1-21","Revelation 17:1-18","Revelation 18:1-24","Revelation 19:1-21","Revelation 1:1-20","Revelation 20:1-15","Revelation 21:1-27","Revelation 22:1-21","Revelation 2:1-29","Revelation 3:1-22","Revelation 5:1-14","Revelation 6:1-17","Revelation 7:1-17","Revelation 8:1-13","Revelation 9:1-21"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_revelation_004_5cf99691eb39cbaad81cf129"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}